Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 123, "itemDescription": "Going by the common moniker MassMutual, the company offers diverse insurance and financial coverages including life insurance, disability overage, and 401k plans. MassMutual estimates it will pay out more than $1.7 billion in dividends to policyholders in 2021."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 336, "itemDescription": "Profits at MassMutual soared 830% year-over-year in 2019, driven by growth in its life insurance, annuities, and customized business services offerings. On top of that, its total assets jumped 10%, to $280 billion, which the insurer credits to its diverse product offerings and investment approach. MassMutual is leveraging its strong financial position to pay the premiums for $3 billion worth of life insurance benefits for health care workers across the U.S. on the front lines of the coronavirus pandemic, effectively insuring them for free."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 89, "itemDescription": "Profits at MassMutual soared 830% year-over-year in 2019\u2014the eighth-biggest jump among <em>Fortune</em> 500 firms\u2014driven by growth in its life insurance, annuities, and customized business services offerings. On top of that, its total assets jumped 10% to $280 billion, which the insurer credits to its diverse product offerings and investment approach. MassMutual is leveraging its strong financial position to pay the premiums for $3 billion worth of life insurance benefits for health care workers across the U.S. on the front lines of the coronavirus pandemic, effectively insuring them for free."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies",